  "body": "## What changed\n\nRotary Offset Zigzag levels now finish their walls with a ring, as the\nplanar #3129 levels already do. On the wrap the plan drops only the\nseam's own edges: a boundary loop that spans a whole period wraps the\nseam, and its two cover-end edges are the seam's two copies at one\nazimuth. That loop's ring keeps one period of boundary per leftover arc;\neach arc arrives open and ends on the seam copy of its start azimuth -\nclosed on the work - while the rows cut the seam columns. A loop that\nwraps no azimuth closes exactly as the planar ring always did. The\nno-seam path is byte-for-byte the old `zigzag_ringed_passes` behaviour.\n\nBefore the fix the wrap kept its rows alone, so every wall perpendicular\nto the rows kept cusps between row ends. Measured on the new test's\nD-flat: the worst wall scallop falls from 0.071 mm to under 0.02 mm at\nevery level between the flat and the skin.\n\nPlacement: `machining2d::pocket_zigzag::ringed_passes` (the seam law,\none `Option<f64>` period), called from `machining3d::hsm::plan_level`.\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/3168-rotary-zigzag-seam-rings.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nNew suite `crates/motion/tests/rotary_zigzag_rings.rs`:\n\n- `the_wrapped_ring_cuts_no_azimuth_twice` - on a developed cover two\n  periods wide, the target band's ring cuts every azimuth once: no\n  azimuth bin takes radial feed runs in both directions, and the band's\n  walls stay within the wall-reach bound. This is the failure the old\n  \"a ring there would cut one seam line twice\" comment feared.\n- `the_dflat_edge_walls_are_ringed` - a D-flat bar wraps and its edge\n  walls (perpendicular to the rows) finish within the wall-reach bound\n  at every level between the flat and the skin. Run against the unfixed\n  tree it fails with `scallop 0.071 mm`.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- The Adaptive seam law (`Seam::crossed_by`, the named refusals) is\n  untouched and its own suites still cover it.\n- No posted G-code golden was re-recorded; the change alters Zigzag\n  wrap toolpaths by adding rings, which the level law's own tests do not\n  pin.\n- The heavy lanes reached by a `motion` diff were not run locally; the\n  review runs them per AGENTS.md.\n\nChangelog: Rotary Offset Zigzag levels finish their walls with a closing\nring that skips the seam, removing wall cusps on flats and other\nperpendicular walls.\n\nfork synced at v0.25.0\n\nFixes #3168\n",
